> 
> The docking station out was working, albeit way to loud. Changing the
> Intel ICH6 SigmaTel STAC9750,51 IEC958 Playback AC97-SPSA tristate
> control from full to anything other muted the output.

Interesting.  Usually AC97-SPSA specifies the AC97 slot for SPDIF
output.  The full (= 3) means the slot 10/11, 0 means slot 3/4.
IIUC, AC97-SPSA must be 3 for docking station output working?

If yes, try to set spdif_aclink=1 with the latest driver (HG
version)...


